[{:seon.task/name "the-turn-shows-how-main-diverged"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `:will-merge` (`seon.merge/divergence` against the agent's merge base) shows what the branch carries; nothing shows what main changed since that base, so a coming conflict is met only at merge. Correct (DESIGN-tasks §3.6, prototyped): one producer of main's changes since the base intersected with the branch's, shown every turn as {:main-ahead n :conflict [..] :you-call [..] :other n} (about 30 tokens): changed by both, changed on main and called by the branch's changes (:form/refs), the rest counted. Its cost follows the changes since the base, not the program (0.4-0.6 ms with a changed-keys index; a full scan 31 ms per db), so it needs the changed-since primitive of seon.merge/program-cost-follows-what-changed."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.context-test/a-turn-names-mains-coming-conflict}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-first-turns-context-costs-what-it-shows"
  :seon.task/plan "Left by a-ranking-takes-each-key-once (2026-10-23, REPL on Seon's own program): the first turn's context for seon.source/an-import-reads-only-changed-files costs 14.3M ticks and 59 MB for an 11 KB text; of the rest, found's pairs query is ~1.9M, ```seon.ref/references``` ~2.1M, then the cited sections and the printing. Measure each part with a cost proof on a production-shaped db, and bring the render to the work its shown text needs."
